title: The Land Question
card-image: img/cards/agricultural_policy.svg?v=2
subtitle: Land committees now, or wait for the Constituent Assembly.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: agricultural_policy_timer <= 0 and land_decree = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; agricultural_policy_timer = 3

The peasants want the landlords' land, and some of them are taking it. The SR minister Chernov wants to regulate the transfers through the land committees; the Kadets say that nothing should be done until the Assembly meets. (Land pressure: [+ land_pressure : level +].)

- @committees: Back the land committees' temporary transfers now.
- @wait: Wait for the Constituent Assembly.
- @reform: Move state and Church lands to the committees at once.
- @easy_discard

@committees

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @committees_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @committees_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @committees_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.

@committees_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: -10, rel_kad: -6, rel_ally: 3, right_threat: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 3, soldiers: 2});
Q.land_committees = (Q.land_committees || 0) + 1;
});
!}

The land committees regulate the transfers of land until the Assembly meets. Landowners are alarmed, and so are their friends in the officer corps. It was phased in slowly, with compensation where it was owed, and the opposition grumbled rather than raged.



@committees_decree
subtitle: The law as written. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: -10, rel_kad: -6, rel_ally: 3, right_threat: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 3, soldiers: 2});
Q.land_committees = (Q.land_committees || 0) + 1;
});
!}

The land committees regulate the transfers of land until the Assembly meets. Landowners are alarmed, and so are their friends in the officer corps.



@committees_force
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Chance of breaking its opponents: Kadets [+ odds_kad +]%, generals [+ odds_gen +]%. A camp under 45% is too strong to touch, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: -10, rel_kad: -6, rel_ally: 3, right_threat: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 3, soldiers: 2});
Q.land_committees = (Q.land_committees || 0) + 1;
});
!}

The land committees regulate the transfers of land until the Assembly meets. Landowners are alarmed, and so are their friends in the officer corps. [+ law_text +]

@wait
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: 3, rel_kad: 3, right_threat: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -2, middle: 1});
!}

The land question will be settled by the Constituent Assembly. The peasants say that they are tired of waiting.

@reform

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @reform_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @reform_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @reform_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.

@reform_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: -4, rel_kad: -2, rel_ally: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 1});
Q.land_committees = (Q.land_committees || 0) + 1;
});
!}

State, appanage and Church lands were put at the committees' disposal. The private estates are still untouched. It is a gesture, and the peasants know it. It was phased in slowly, with compensation where it was owed, and the opposition grumbled rather than raged.



